thor"><name><surname>Layard</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><source>Happiness: lessons from a new science</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Penguin Press</publisher-name><fpage>ix, 310</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003985-Rotter1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rotter</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><year>1967</year><article-title>A new scale for the measurement of interpersonal trust.</article-title><source>J Pers</source><volume>35</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>665</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4865583</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003985-Suedfeld1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Suedfeld</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Soriano</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>McMurtry</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiszbeck</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Erikson's &#x0201c;components of a healthy personality&#x0201d; among Holocaust survivors immediately and 40 years after the war.</article-title><source>Int J Aging Hum Dev</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>248</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15934215</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003985-Gallo1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gallo</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>TW</given-names></name><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Socioeconomic status, psychosocial processes, and perceived health: an interpersonal persp